# Authenticated plain-text clipboard

Branch: macos-host-clipboard. Baseline: release 1.0.135.

## Scope

Add macOS Host ↔ macOS Client plain UTF-8 clipboard, retaining Mac Client ↔
Linux X11 Host. No files, images, rich text, new ports, Linux Client backend,
login-screen clipboard or permission bypass. Maximum encoded text: 512 KiB.

## Implementation

1. Share bounded wire/UTF-8 validation across the native Mac Host and existing
   endpoints. Keep platform clipboard ownership separate from transport.
2. Reject oversize, embedded NUL and invalid UTF-8 before outgoing allocation;
   never truncate or log contents. Retry queue pressure from the unsent chunk,
   without restarting a generation or disconnecting video.
3. Bound clipboard work per transport turn. Preserve reliable input ordering,
   particularly clipboard completion before a following paste keystroke.
4. Negotiate clipboard explicitly in the Mac launch contract. Only a negotiated,
   authenticated desktop worker for the active account may access NSPasteboard.
   A Linux Client still connects without negotiating clipboard.
5. Scope pending work to the session; revoke on logout, takeover and teardown.
   Clear only remotely owned pasteboard data, preserving later local copies.
   Do not block capture/input lifecycle on an AppKit permission prompt.

## Validation and handoff

Test Unicode, multiline, exact/over-limit input, malformed chunks, independent
generations, partial-send retry, queue pressure, repeated A→B→A, newer local
ownership, background focus and session replacement. Keep existing Xvfb and
native Client regressions. Add Mac Host native tests with an isolated pasteboard
and fake session authority; never overwrite a runner/user's general clipboard.

Build branch-qualified Host/Client candidates on hosted builders. Compilation
is not live acceptance: paired Mac copy/paste, Linux regression, Spaces, user
transitions and permission denial require interactive qualification. Do not
merge or publish a release before acceptance.
